<file path=".serena/memories/AGENTS.md">
# Serena memory graph contract

## Purpose

These files let an AI with zero repository context load only the minimum durable knowledge needed for its task. They are a directed retrieval graph, not a duplicate wiki, task log, or prompt dump.

## Required flat graph

```text
mem:eme_core
├── mem:eme_project_overview
├── mem:eme_architecture_authority
├── mem:eme_architecture_ownership
├── mem:eme_engineering_commands
├── mem:eme_engineering_completion
└── mem:eme_engineering_toolchain
```

- Every project memory is a flat file named `eme_<area>_<topic>.md`: lower-case ASCII and underscores only. No project-memory subdirectories.
- `mem:eme_core` is the only mandatory entry point. It contains routing triggers and no detailed implementation facts.
- Each child has exactly one primary question. It contains dense, stable answers and may link only to a narrower necessary child.
- `memory_maintenance.md` is the one reserved Serena file-name exception: Serena creates and reads it during onboarding. Do not rename it to an `eme_` name.
- Future knowledge uses the same flat scheme, for example `eme_domain_attendance.md`, `eme_app_web.md`, `eme_integration_line.md`, `eme_operation_release.md`, or `eme_decision_identity_isolation.md`.

## Content constraints

- Add only durable, non-obvious facts that prevent costly rediscovery and have a real future consumer.
- Source of truth remains repository code, manifests, schemas, tests, and architecture authority. Never copy large authorities or replace them with prose summaries.
- Do not store temporary status, chat history, branch/SHA-specific evidence, raw command output, credentials, personal data, or generic framework knowledge.
- Parents state when a child is relevant. Children state facts only; they do not repeat task workflow or global instructions.
- References must use backticked `mem:<name>` syntax and target an existing flat memory name, for example `mem:eme_architecture_authority`. Do not create duplicate memories for the same question.

## Mutation constraints

1. Read `mem:eme_core` and `mem:memory_maintenance` before adding or changing a memory.
2. Reuse the existing owner; create a new file only when no current node can own the fact without gaining a second responsibility.
3. Rename through Serena's memory rename operation when available; otherwise update every incoming `mem:` reference atomically.
4. After every graph change, run `serena memories check`. Do not claim the graph is usable if that check reports a broken reference.
</file>

<file path="apps/web/src/app/(rich-menu)/AGENTS.md">
# Rich Menu route group

`(rich-menu)` owns authenticated LINE Rich Menu navigation composition at the
Web route-group boundary. It maps Rich Menu actions to existing canonical
application surfaces and preserves direct-entry and authentication continuity.

## Boundary

- This route group is parallel to `(mobile)` and does not enter the URL.
- It does not own business truth, authorization, persistence, Attendance,
  Notifications, Repository, Profile, or LINE provider configuration.
- Reuse the existing owner contract and canonical route before adding a new
  destination, adapter, writer, or business abstraction.
- Presentation labels and query parameters express navigation intent only;
  they never authorize or create a new source of truth.
- LINE Rich Menu definition, publication, rollback, and provider readback stay
  with `packages/line` and the canonical LINE operations.

## Navigation invariants

- Every action resolves to one canonical application surface.
- `/profile` resolves the current authenticated User entry; it must not create
  a second Profile surface or regress to Settings.
- Attendance-backed Time Tracking reuses the Attendance application contract and
  preserves qualification, replay, version, isolation, transaction, and
  recovery semantics.
- Notifications remain recipient-scoped and owner-authoritative.
- Direct entry, refresh, back navigation, and authenticated continuation must
  converge on the same owner semantics.

## Change and validation

Before changing a destination, confirm its canonical URL, business/data owner,
public contract, authorization behavior, direct-entry behavior, and existing
consumer. Do not duplicate an existing resource route.

Run the affected route and owner tests, then applicable `pnpm lint`,
`pnpm typecheck` and `pnpm test`. Use provider readback for actual Rich
Menu publication; local route checks do not prove provider publication.
</file>

<file path="apps/web/src/app/AGENTS.md">
# App route scope

`apps/web/src/app` 擁有 Next.js route ownership、layout、HTTP delivery 與最外層 composition。Business truth、authorization、resource lifecycle 與 persistence 仍由 owning package/application contract 決定。

## Route invariants

- 一個正式 URL 只有一個 route owner；Route Group 只表達 layout/runtime responsibility，不進 URL、也不授權。
- Page / Route Handler 只做 transport、presentation 與 composition；不得複製 Domain/Application rule 或直接建立第二個 writer。
- Stable ID、login、slug、number 與 query parameter只定位／表達 intent；不能自稱 actor、scope、role、permission 或 current version。
- Direct open、refresh、soft navigation、back 與登入接續必須回到同一 authoritative query/command semantics。
- 任意 `returnUrl`、credential、private draft、authorization decision 或 mutable server state 不進產品 URL。
- `app/api/_composition` 只在最外層接 concrete adapters；module/shared 不反向依賴 app composition。

Current route inventory、Mobile app-shell 與 URL contract 由 [Web runtime](../../../../docs/reference/runtime/routes.md) 與實際 route tree共同證明；本檔不再手抄第二份 route/feature清單。

## Scope routing

| Scope | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| [(public)](%28public%29/AGENTS.md) | Public entry 與 public locator delivery |
| [(resource)](%28resource%29/AGENTS.md) | Canonical resource URL / projection |
| [(mobile)](%28mobile%29/AGENTS.md) | Authenticated Mobile / LINE MINI App delivery |
| [(rich-menu)](%28rich-menu%29/AGENTS.md) | Rich Menu entry composition |
| [(onboarding)](%28onboarding%29/AGENTS.md) | Registration / restore / completion |
| [(system)](%28system%29/AGENTS.md) | Callback / continuation / unavailable results |
| [api](api/AGENTS.md) | HTTP methods、input/scope translation、owner wiring |

FPT domain-truth / GitHub Mobile benchmark usage 繼承 [apps scope](../../../AGENTS.md)。GitHub-derived locator field semantics 必須直接引用 FPT；實際 route ownership、authorization 與 activation 仍由本地 semantic owner/runtime contract 決定，不從 GitHub URL 形狀推導。

## Change rules

- 修改 URL 前沿 `page/route → module → _composition → package public export` 查實際 consumer，同時檢查 direct open、refresh、back、login/LIFF continuation 與舊入口。
- 新增 framework special file、parallel/intercepting route 或 slot 必須有真實 navigation/runtime responsibility；不為形式完整預建。
- Protected request 每次重新驗可信 identity / qualification / scope；layout、page visibility、query 或 prior success 都不能替代 authorization。
- External callback/webhook 按 provider trust contract 驗證；credential 不複製到產品 URL。
- 未實作能力留在 Governance / semantic status，不建立空 page/API 宣稱完成。

## Naming

- route segment 與 Next.js special file 是 delivery contract；只能在已同步 URL consumer 與 navigation 行為的變更中調整。
- route group 用 layout/runtime 責任命名，不以業務 owner、資料表或暫時頁面狀態命名。

相關 current contract：[Web runtime](../../../../docs/reference/runtime/routes.md)；repository placement：[Dependency boundaries](../../../../docs/rules/dependency-boundaries.md)。
</file>

